Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedshaker.shoddy — reckoner seed: shaker.shoddy, converting at
Rem the bridge
Rem
Rem SHAKE, UNSHAKE, UNSHAKEOR, SHAKEOK and SHAKEMOD. Per R4.16 there is
Rem no ARRAY cell at the keyboard: a message or a key list is a LIST of
Rem NUMBERs on the way in and out, exactly as shaker.shoddy itself wants
Rem — this machine already deals in nothing but numbers.
Rem
Rem SHAKE and UNSHAKE pre-flight the exact conditions ShakeEncrypt and
Rem ShakeDecrypt themselves Error on — an empty key, a key or message
Rem value outside the field, a checksum that does not match — and
Rem refuse by name instead, the same guard-before-abort discipline every
Rem other seed applies to the machine underneath it. UNSHAKEOR and
Rem SHAKEOK need no guard of their own: shaker.shoddy already made both
Rem total.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "shaker.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- a LIST cell as List Of Number ----------------------------------

Def ShListNum(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(xs)
            ShNumsAt(word, xs, { })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def ShNumsAt(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number) As Result
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        ShNumsNext(word, xs, acc, First(xs))

Def ShNumsNext(word As String, xs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            ShNumsAt(word, Rest(xs), Append(acc, x))
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "a LIST of NUMBERs", c), 0)

Rem Both arguments read as List Of Number before either machine word
Rem sees them, so a wrong-shaped list is refused by this seed rather
Rem than reaching shaker.shoddy at all.
Def ShTwoLists(word As String, a As Cell, b As Cell) As Result
    Select Case ShListNum(word, a)
        Case Ok(xs)
            ShTwoListsWith(word, xs, b)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def ShTwoListsWith(word As String, xs As List Of Number, b As Cell) As Result
    Select Case ShListNum(word, b)
        Case Ok(ys)
            Ok({ xs, ys })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- SHAKE ------------------------------------------------------------
Rem The three conditions ShakeEncrypt itself Errors on, checked here so
Rem a bad call refuses instead: an empty key, a key value outside the
Rem field, a message value outside the field.

Def ShSeedShake(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SHAKE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => ShShake(vs)), "( list keys -- cipher )", "The list, obfuscated under keys — one value longer, the last a tamper checksum.")

Def ShShake(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ShTwoLists("SHAKE", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(pair)
            ShShakeChecked(Nth(pair, 1), Nth(pair, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SHAKE did not answer")

Def ShShakeChecked(xs As List Of Number, keys As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(keys) Then
        RckWorkBad("SHAKE: THE KEY IS EMPTY")
    Else
        If Not ShakeAllField(keys) Then
            RckWorkBad("SHAKE: EVERY KEY VALUE MUST BE A WHOLE NUMBER IN 0 .. " & Str(ShakeModulus() - 1))
        Else
            If Not ShakeAllField(xs) Then
                RckWorkBad("SHAKE: EVERY MESSAGE VALUE MUST BE A WHOLE NUMBER IN 0 .. " & Str(ShakeModulus() - 1))
            Else
                RckVals({ CutList(Map(ShakeEncrypt(xs, keys), CutNum)) })

Rem ---- UNSHAKE ------------------------------------------------------------
Rem Strict, matching ShakeDecrypt: an empty key or a checksum mismatch
Rem refuses rather than answering rubbish.

Def ShSeedUnshake(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "UNSHAKE", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => ShUnshake(vs)), "( cipher keys -- list )", "The message SHAKE produced, or a refusal if the key is empty or the checksum does not match.")

Def ShUnshake(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ShTwoLists("UNSHAKE", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(pair)
            ShUnshakeChecked(Nth(pair, 1), Nth(pair, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("UNSHAKE did not answer")

Def ShUnshakeChecked(xs As List Of Number, keys As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If IsEmpty(keys) Then
        RckWorkBad("UNSHAKE: THE KEY IS EMPTY")
    Else
        If Not ShakeAllField(keys) Then
            RckWorkBad("UNSHAKE: EVERY KEY VALUE MUST BE A WHOLE NUMBER IN 0 .. " & Str(ShakeModulus() - 1))
        Else
            If Not ShakeVerify(xs) Then
                RckWorkBad("UNSHAKE: CHECKSUM MISMATCH — THE MESSAGE WAS ALTERED OR IS NOT A CIPHERTEXT")
            Else
                RckVals({ CutList(Map(ShakeDecrypt(xs, keys), CutNum)) })

Rem ---- UNSHAKEOR ----------------------------------------------------------
Rem Already total in shaker.shoddy, so this is the plain three-argument
Rem bridge and nothing more.

Def ShSeedUnshakeor(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "UNSHAKEOR", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => ShUnshakeor(vs)), "( cipher keys dflt -- list )", "UNSHAKE, or dflt unchanged when the key is empty, out of field, or the checksum does not match.")

Def ShUnshakeor(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ShTwoLists("UNSHAKEOR", Nth(vs, 1), Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Ok(pair)
            ShUnshakeorChecked(Nth(pair, 1), Nth(pair, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("UNSHAKEOR did not answer")

Def ShUnshakeorChecked(xs As List Of Number, keys As List Of Number, dflt As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ShListNum("UNSHAKEOR", dflt)
        Case Ok(ds)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(ShakeDecryptOr(xs, keys, ds), CutNum)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("UNSHAKEOR did not answer")

Rem ---- SHAKEOK ------------------------------------------------------------
Rem ShakeVerify is already total — False for anything too short to
Rem carry a checksum, never a refusal.

Def ShSeedShakeok(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SHAKEOK", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => ShShakeok(vs)), "( list -- flag )", "Whether the checksum SHAKE appended still matches the body.")

Def ShShakeok(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ShListNum("SHAKEOK", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(xs)
            RckVals({ CutBool(ShakeVerify(xs)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SHAKEOK did not answer")

Rem ---- SHAKEMOD -----------------------------------------------------------

Def ShSeedShakemod(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SHAKEMOD", 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(ShakeModulus()) })), "( -- n )", "The field size: every SHAKE value is a whole number in 0 .. n-1.")

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedShaker(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = ShSeedShake(st)
    Let s2 = ShSeedUnshake(s1)
    Let s3 = ShSeedUnshakeor(s2)
    Let s4 = ShSeedShakeok(s3)
    ShSeedShakemod(s4)
